From 90087807b03162987eee2abeea3893b9f41fa60b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 20:40:43 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] WebPlayer: play web pages through a resident web client

Kodi has no way to show a web page. Add a player core that shows one
through a web client hosted by the Wayland host. CWebClientManager, an
application component, runs the host for Kodi's lifetime, starts the
client named by web.clientcommand once the GUI is up (web.enabled,
web.preload), waits for kodi_web_v1 ready, restarts a client that was
up once and stays failed after a second loss until the next web
request. The client keeps its data under special://profile/webdata and
its cache under special://temp/webcache through XDG_DATA_HOME and
XDG_CACHE_HOME, so profile data follows the Kodi profile.

The player asks the manager for the view of the item's web.profile
property, loads the URL into it, activates it, and feeds the frames the
view commits to the render manager as DRM PRIME pictures, so the
existing renderers show them and the GUI composes over the page like
over any video; the view's frame callbacks complete on Kodi's render
loop, which paces the client to the display. On stop the view is
deactivated and loads about:blank, so the next page opens at once. The
player is registered as "WebPlayer" of type "web" and selected through
JSON-RPC Player.Open with playername. Kodi neither probes an item
addressed to it as a playlist nor looks up its MIME type or resolves
its path, since each would fetch the page through Kodi's HTTP client
before the view loads it.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
